## Project scope notes

The notes below explain the intended scope of this repository's MIT notice.
They do not replace the license text above or grant rights to material owned
by third parties.
### Repository-owned code

The MIT grant applies to code and documentation authored for this repository
by the copyright holder, subject to the license conditions above. It does not
transfer ownership of the project or require attribution beyond retaining the
copyright and permission notice in copies or substantial portions.
### Duplicate neural-network example

The extensionless file bpalgo and the Python entry point bpalgo.py contain the
same demonstration code in the current repository. The same repository
copyright and MIT notice apply to both copies.
### Generated synthetic values

id3.py generates its demonstration rows at runtime from NumPy random values.
Those generated values are not a separately curated third-party dataset. Any
new data added later should carry its own source and permission information.
### Dependencies

Streamlit, NumPy, pandas, Python, and other tools used to run the examples are
maintained separately and are not relicensed by this file. Their own copyright
notices and license terms continue to apply to those packages.
